  "name": "Sandbag Barrier",
  "class": "large_prop",
  "slot": "barrier",
  "mass": 900,
  "_note": "The first buildable, and the asset C4 was arguing about when it reserved `build` to C5: *a sandbag wall that does not topple sideways where a clay one slumps is a prop with a placement cost.* It topples now \u2014 `support_lateral` on sandbag is 8, which is what makes a parapet come apart into bags rather than slump as a mass \u2014 so the argument is paid for and the verb can go live.",
  "_cost": "`spoil: 4` is four spade-bites of earth, and it comes out of the ground you are standing on. That is the loop EARTH-SPEC \u00a74 has been building toward since C3: digging produces spoil, spoil is what a parapet is made of, and the hole and the wall are the same act seen from two sides.",
